WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Democrats take over of Congress will shape U.S. policy on Iran and Ukraine for the next two years. This is Omni View, episode 226. Indonesia's appeal to Moscow, a pollution lawsuit in Congo, and Eurozone inflation follow, then understanding the issue. Democrats in a result CNBC framed as voters delivering a direct setback to President Trump's legislative agenda that now threatens to constrain his ability to advance his priorities. Took majorities in both the Senate and the House of Representatives

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.940
by flipping seats and states that had been held by Republicans, with projections showing at least 54 Senate seats and

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:43.680
225 House seats after wins in Texas, North Carolina, Ohio, Michigan, Kansas and Maine.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:51.580
James Tallerico defeated Republican Ken Paxton and became the first Democrat in 38 years to take a Texas Senate seat

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:57.720
and Gina Hinojosa unceded Republican Greg Abbott to become Texas's first Latina governor.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:03.600
While in Kansas, Adam Hamilton became the first Democrat to win a Senate seat since 1932.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:09.120
North Carolina elected former Democratic Governor Roy Cooper over Trump-backed Michael

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.420
Watley for a Senate seat.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:16.200
Ohio returned former Democratic Senator Sherrod Brown over Republican incumbent John Houston.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.740
Maine's progressive Troy Jackson ended Republican Susan Collins' three decades in office.

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:27.660
US. Michigan chose Abdul-El-Sayed for its open Senate seat, and Georgia re-elected Democratic

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:32.960
Senator John Assoff as former Atlanta Mayor Keisha Lance Bottoms became the first black

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:38.460
woman elected governor of any US state. The Guardian described the result as a blue wave

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:44.180
driven by voter concerns over the cost of living, inflation, and the war in Iran, highlighting

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:49.380
the scale of historic firsts across federal and state races, among them the election of

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:53.500
first Muslim Senator. Reuters recorded immediate reactions from foreign

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:57.840
capitals, with European officials noting the shift could alter the tone of US

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.220
engagement on climate policy, while leaving the president's core foreign policy

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.715
powers intact. Indonesia's foreign ministry, the South China Morning Post, reported,

00:02:08.275 --> 00:02:12.175
asked Russia on Sunday through standard diplomatic channels to stop recruiting

00:02:12.175 --> 00:02:16.235
Indonesian nationals to fight in Ukraine. After reports that Indonesian

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:21.575
citizens were being approached for military contracts. Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Yvonne

00:02:21.575 --> 00:02:26.155
Meweng-Kang stated that the government asked Russia to take all necessary steps to ensure

00:02:26.155 --> 00:02:31.715
no Indonesians are recruited into the Russian military, or any other entity involved in the conflict.

00:02:32.135 --> 00:02:37.395
A request that reaches the army and other groups tied to the fighting. Analysts believe that appeal

00:02:37.395 --> 00:02:43.335
is unlikely to succeed unless President Prabowo Subianto raises the issue directly with Vladimir Putin.

00:02:43.335 --> 00:02:48.635
Because a ministry note uses the routine path between governments and does not tap the

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:50.655
personal relationship between the two leaders.

00:02:51.275 --> 00:02:55.875
A direct presidential intervention would carry more weight than routine diplomatic messaging,

00:02:56.355 --> 00:03:01.135
those analysts observed, which is why they treat a Sunday channel message as weaker than a

00:03:01.135 --> 00:03:03.895
conversation Proboeul himself might have with Putin.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:11.110
Residents of Colwezi, France 24's correspondent reported, filed a lawsuit against a major Chinese

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:16.250
his own mind and Congolese authorities, alleging widespread environmental damage from mining

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.850
operations in the mining capital of the Democratic Republic of Congo.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:25.230
Pollution is affecting communities that live alongside those operations, and the people

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.550
who brought the case seek accountability for that harm rather than a quiet settlement out

00:03:29.550 --> 00:03:30.310
of public view.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:35.130
The correspondence said the suit will be one of the most important environmental cases the

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:40.330
country has seen, a rank that reflects how wide the alleged damage runs and how rarely a

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:45.090
case of this size reaches a courtroom there. The proceedings will test the legal systems

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:50.370
capacity to address large-scale industrial impacts, and that test now sits with judges

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:54.830
who must weigh a Chinese-owned operator and Congolese authorities in the same filing.

00:03:55.731 --> 00:04:01.431
Eurozone inflation climbed for a fourth consecutive month and reached 4%, the Wall Street Journal

00:04:01.431 --> 00:04:06.231
reporting that higher energy costs were the main driver, and that this is the highest inflation

00:04:06.231 --> 00:04:12.011
reading in three years. The increase followed three prior monthly rises, a run that reinforced

00:04:12.011 --> 00:04:16.571
market expectations that the European Central Bank may need to consider further interest

00:04:16.571 --> 00:04:22.611
rate adjustments after holding its key rate last week. Investing.com likewise tied the rise

00:04:22.611 --> 00:04:28.151
to energy prices and said markets now expect the European Central Bank to consider further interest

00:04:28.151 --> 00:04:34.744
rate adjustments, with the latest figures able to influence upcoming policy decisions. Investors pushed

00:04:34.744 --> 00:04:40.384
major equity indices higher. AP News reporting broad-based advances across regions as the

00:04:40.384 --> 00:04:46.044
new lineup in Washington came into view. Reduced uncertainty over US fiscal policy was cited

00:04:46.044 --> 00:04:50.964
as a supporting factor in that movement, and investors appeared to respond positively to the

00:04:50.964 --> 00:04:57.108
clearer picture of divided government in Washington. BMW lowered its profit outlook again, citing

00:04:57.108 --> 00:05:02.628
higher restructuring costs. A fresh warning Reuters said follows earlier cautions from the company

00:05:02.628 --> 00:05:06.108
and reflects ongoing adjustments in its European operations.

00:05:06.708 --> 00:05:09.488
The carmaker is still working to streamline manufacturing

00:05:09.488 --> 00:05:11.628
and to respond to shifting demand patterns.

00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:14.628
And those restructuring costs are what the company says

00:05:14.628 --> 00:05:19.394
are weighing on profit. Hong Kong, the South China Morning Post reported,

00:05:19.914 --> 00:05:22.874
opened the first overseas office of the International Institute

00:05:22.874 --> 00:05:26.274
for the Unification of Private Law, progress worth knowing

00:05:26.274 --> 00:05:29.174
in a city already described as a legal exchange hub

00:05:29.174 --> 00:05:31.114
with strong ties to mainland China.

00:05:31.114 --> 00:05:36.094
4. Former Justice Minister Theresa Chang, now Secretary-General for the International

00:05:36.094 --> 00:05:42.014
Organization for Mediation, said the move underscores that hub role, and the office is expected

00:05:42.014 --> 00:05:46.814
to facilitate cross-border legal cooperation under Hong Kong's existing legal framework.

00:05:47.514 --> 00:05:52.354
Coverage of the opening stressed the city's importance for legal exchange, supported by a broad

00:05:52.354 --> 00:05:57.494
legal system and those mainland connections, as a private law body plants its first office

00:05:57.494 --> 00:06:03.184
outside its home base. Elsewhere, an Indonesian military helicopter, the South China Morning

00:06:03.184 --> 00:06:08.424
Post reported, crashed off Borneo during firefighting operations and killed one crew member.

00:06:09.044 --> 00:06:13.584
The Australian government defended its social media age limit in court, with lawyers

00:06:13.584 --> 00:06:19.444
Al Jazeera noted, arguing that a ban for under-16s is needed to protect children. Spain's

00:06:19.444 --> 00:06:24.444
transport minister resigned after a train crash that killed 69 people. The resignation

00:06:24.444 --> 00:06:29.854
coming after two major accidents in under a year. Midterm coverage often treats a

00:06:29.854 --> 00:06:34.694
congressional win as one event, yet each chamber has its own rulebook for how fast a

00:06:34.694 --> 00:06:38.634
party can rewrite the law, and to really understand the mechanism, you have to

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:42.994
watch the house and the Senate as different machines. The House of Representatives has

00:06:43.534 --> 00:06:48.774
435 voting seats, each representing a district of roughly equal population, and

00:06:48.774 --> 00:06:52.954
every one of those seats is contested every two years, so the full membership can

00:06:52.954 --> 00:06:54.634
beyond the ballot in a single cycle.

00:06:55.074 --> 00:07:00.594
The Senate has 100 seats, with one third of members elected every six years, giving that

00:07:00.594 --> 00:07:04.954
chamber greater continuity than the House and spreading change across several elections

00:07:04.954 --> 00:07:06.014
instead of one night.

00:07:06.574 --> 00:07:11.454
Because most seats are safely held by one party, control usually hinges on a small number

00:07:11.454 --> 00:07:16.054
of competitive districts and states, and the Guardian's Interactive Results page explains

00:07:16.054 --> 00:07:21.614
that experts classify only a handful of races as genuine toss-ups each cycle, which is

00:07:21.614 --> 00:07:24.554
This is why a shift of just a few seats can flip an entire chamber.

00:07:25.114 --> 00:07:30.474
Before the election, the Cook report classified six Senate races as genuine toss-ups, while

00:07:30.474 --> 00:07:34.574
Democrats were favored in enough house seats to take the chamber without winning any of

00:07:34.574 --> 00:07:40.374
the 18 seats the Cook political report classed as toss-ups, and 33 of the 100 Senate seats

00:07:40.374 --> 00:07:42.954
were up for election along with two special elections.

00:07:43.594 --> 00:07:49.014
Republicans were defending a majority in the House, where Democrats held 212 seats and needed

00:07:49.014 --> 00:07:50.614
218 for control.

00:07:51.374 --> 00:07:56.374
Gubernatorial elections were taking place in 36 states, and a large popular vote margin

00:07:56.374 --> 00:07:59.894
does not automatically translate into proportional legislative power.

00:08:00.394 --> 00:08:05.614
So when a claim lands that one party now controls everything, check whether the account distinguishes

00:08:05.614 --> 00:08:08.954
the short-term house majority from the longer-term senate calendar.

00:08:10.247 --> 00:08:15.027
CNBC's photo essay presents the election through images and a result summary from key races.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:19.567
sources, while the Guardian's live blog stays with rolling analysis and reaction from

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:20.507
foreign governments.

00:08:21.027 --> 00:08:25.607
State authorities will release certified canvassing reports and congressional seat totals,

00:08:26.087 --> 00:08:28.887
the primary record to set against election night projections.

00:08:29.447 --> 00:08:34.727
That's omniview, as always, compare outlets, look for primary documents, and separate

00:08:34.727 --> 00:08:36.227
what's known from what's assumed.

00:08:36.787 --> 00:08:41.327
The world is complicated, but it's not beyond understanding, and you just spend a few minutes

00:08:41.327 --> 00:08:42.407
understanding it better.

